# recomp_lift manifest for Juiced 1.00 (work/Juiced.exe from tools/prepare-exe.sh). Each entry says why.
# CPU feature probe (stdcall, one argument: 1 MMX, 2 SSE, 4 SSE2, 8 3DNow!,
# 0x10.. SSE3 and later): runs the feature's instruction under SEH and returns
# whether it did not fault. Lifted code cannot fault on an unimplemented
# instruction, so src/hooks.cpp answers for the runtime's CPU: SSE and SSE2 only.
replace 005A16D0 CpuFeatureProbe
# Texture load by name (this = esi, the name the second stack argument): src/hooks.cpp shows the pad's button
# pictures for the menus' keyboard hints while a pad is connected.
replace 00510090 TextureLoad
# Fitting a car's catalogue parts into a copy of its model's dynamics (edi the car, esi the dynamics; OpenJuice's fit,
# 0x0048E380 in its EXE): src/hooks.cpp adds an overdrive bought in the tuning menu (gearbox part byte 0x7F, 0x7E).
replace 0048DFE0 FitParts
# The overdrive's sale (src/hooks.cpp): tuningmenu's enter and update (this = ecx, the window the argument), and
# gearboxmenu's update, whose gearing purchase writes the gearbox part 1.
replace 0043A890 TuningMenuEnter
replace 0043A9C0 TuningMenuUpdate
replace 004427C0 GearboxMenuUpdate
# performtype's enter and update (this = ecx, the window the argument): the overdrive's levels (src/hooks.cpp).
replace 00441670 PerformTypeEnter
replace 00441910 PerformTypeUpdate
# Smarter AI (src/ai.cpp)
hook 0049B20E ai_line
hook 0049DE58 ai_brake
hook 0049CB93 ai_dodge
hook 0049CCCB ai_dodge_end
